    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Pydantic is the most widely used data-validation library for Python. It validates",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "data at runtime against Python type hints and produces structured, user-friendly",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "errors when data is invalid. Pydantic v2 (released mid-2023, stable and current",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "through 2026) rewrote the validation/serialization engine in Rust as a separate",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "package, pydantic-core (built with PyO3). The result is ~5–50× faster than",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "v1 (≈17× on a typical mixed-field model), with the Python layer reduced to schema",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "definition while the hot path runs in compiled Rust.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Three packages make up the ecosystem:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "pydantic - the Python API (BaseModel, Field, validators, TypeAdapter).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "pydantic-core - the Rust validation/serialization engine (not used directly).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "pydantic-settings - BaseSettings for config from env vars, .env, secrets.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use it when you need to parse untrusted input (API bodies, config, JSON, ORM",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "rows) into typed Python objects with guarantees, and serialize them back out.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#overview-1",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. BaseModel and field definitions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Subclass BaseModel; annotate fields with type hints. Validation runs on",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "construction and on the explicit model_validate* entry points.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Validation entry points: User(**data), User.model_validate(dict_or_obj),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "User.model_validate_json(json_str_or_bytes). JSON parsing happens inside Rust",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "in model_validate_json - faster than json.loads() then model_validate.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Field(...) carries metadata/constraints: default, default_factory,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "alias / validation_alias / serialization_alias, ge/gt/le/lt,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "min_length/max_length, pattern, description, frozen, exclude.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Prefer Annotated[type, Field(...)] over field: type = Field(...) for",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "constraints. Constraints inside Annotated are compiled into the core schema and",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "run in Rust (no Python call overhead). They also compose with list[...],",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "dict[...], etc. (e.g. list[Annotated[int, Field(gt=0)]]).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "from_attributes=True (in model_config, replaces v1 orm_mode) lets",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "model_validate read attributes off arbitrary objects (e.g. ORM rows).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#1-basemodel-and-field-definitions",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Validators — field, model, and the before/after/wrap modes",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Pydantic distinguishes validators (input → validated value) from serializers",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(value → output). Validators run in a defined order around the core (Rust) validation.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Modes (the most-confused part of Pydantic v2):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mode=\"before\" - runs on raw input before core coercion. Receives whatever",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "was passed (often a dict or str); use to reshape/normalize input.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mode=\"after\" - runs on the already-validated, typed value. Safest default for",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "business rules; you get a real int/str/submodel, not raw input.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mode=\"wrap\" - most powerful: receives the value and a handler callable; you",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "decide whether/when to call the inner validator and can transform around it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mode=\"plain\" - terminates validation; your function fully replaces core validation",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "for that field (no core coercion runs).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "model_validator(mode=\"before\") receives the raw input dict for the whole model;",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mode=\"after\" receives self (return self). Raise ValueError or AssertionError",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "inside a validator and Pydantic wraps it into a ValidationError. Validators can",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "take an info: ValidationInfo param for info.data (already-validated siblings),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "info.context, info.field_name.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Reusable validators: attach a validator to a type once with",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Annotated[str, AfterValidator(func)] / BeforeValidator / WrapValidator /",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PlainValidator - cleaner than repeating @field_validator across models.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#2-validators-field-model-and-the-beforeafterwrap-modes",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Strict vs lax mode and ConfigDict",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "By default Pydantic is lax: it coerces compatible types (\"123\" → 123,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"true\" → True). Strict mode disables coercion and requires exact types.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Strictness is layered (most → least specific): per-call model_validate(..., strict=True)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> field-level Field(strict=True) / Strict() annotation > model_config.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Common ConfigDict keys:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "strict, frozen (immutable + hashable; replaces v1 allow_mutation),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "extra = \"ignore\" (default) / \"forbid\" / \"allow\",",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "validate_assignment=True (re-validate on attribute set; off by default),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "from_attributes=True (ORM reads), populate_by_name=True (accept field name",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and alias on input; renamed validate_by_name in newer versions),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "str_strip_whitespace, use_enum_values, arbitrary_types_allowed,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "json_schema_extra, ser_json_timedelta, etc.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "model_config is a dict (ConfigDict(...)), not the v1 nested class Config.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#3-strict-vs-lax-mode-and-configdict",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Serialization — model_dump, JSON, aliases, computed fields",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Key options (apply to all three): include / exclude (sets or nested dicts),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "by_alias=True (use serialization_alias), exclude_unset (only fields explicitly",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "set - great for PATCH semantics), exclude_defaults, exclude_none,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "round_trip=True, warnings=\"error\", context=....",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Custom serializers: @field_serializer(\"foo\", mode=\"plain\"|\"wrap\") for one",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "field; @model_serializer for the whole model; Annotated[T, PlainSerializer(...)]",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "for reusable type-level serialization.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "@computed_field - expose a derived @property in the serialized output:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "RootModel[T] - a model whose top level is not an object (e.g.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "RootModel[list[int]], RootModel[dict[str, User]]); replaces v1 __root__.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#4-serialization-model_dump-json-aliases-computed-fields",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. TypeAdapter — validation/serialization without a BaseModel",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "TypeAdapter brings Pydantic's machinery to any type - list[User], dict[str,int],",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#5-typeadapter-validationserialization-without-a-basemodel",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "TypedDict, dataclasses, unions - without wrapping it in a model. Build the adapter",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#5-typeadapter-validationserialization-without-a-basemodel",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "once (it compiles a core schema) and reuse it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#5-typeadapter-validationserialization-without-a-basemodel",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use it for bulk validation of homogeneous collections (build the adapter at module",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#5-typeadapter-validationserialization-without-a-basemodel",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "scope, not per call) and for validating request/response bodies that aren't models.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#5-typeadapter-validationserialization-without-a-basemodel",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Discriminated (tagged) unions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Add a discriminator so the core validator picks one union member by a tag field",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "instead of trying each - faster, and produces one clean error instead of N.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "For tags that aren't a plain field, use a callable discriminator via",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Discriminator(func) - and handle both dict and model inputs inside it, since the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "callable also runs during serialization. Discriminated unions also emit cleaner",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "OpenAPI/JSON-Schema. Non-discriminated unions use smart mode (best-match) by",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "default; left-to-right is available but usually worse.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#6-discriminated-tagged-unions",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. pydantic-settings — typed configuration",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "BaseSettings populates fields from (priority high→low): **init kwargs → env vars →",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": ".env file → secrets dir → field defaults**.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Nested config: env_nested_delimiter=\"__\" maps APP_DB__HOST to db.host",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(double underscore avoids clashing with names that contain single underscores).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Secrets: secrets_dir reads each file as one field's value (Docker/K8s secrets).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Customize sources by overriding settings_customise_sources (e.g. add a YAML or",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "vault source, reorder priority).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Best practice: .env for local dev only, commit a .env.example without",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "secrets, use real environment variables / secret stores in production.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#7-pydantic-settings-typed-configuration",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tools / Frameworks",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "FastAPI - built on Pydantic; request/response models are Pydantic models.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "FastAPI ≥0.100 requires Pydantic v2.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "bump-pydantic - automated V1→V2 codemod (renames @validator→@field_validator,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Config→model_config, .dict()→.model_dump(), etc.). Run it, then review diffs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "datamodel-code-generator - generate Pydantic models from JSON Schema / OpenAPI.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "json_schema() / model_json_schema() - emit JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) for any",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "model or TypeAdapter, including for discriminated unions.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mypy / pyright - Pydantic ships a mypy plugin; v2 models type-check well with",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#tools-frameworks",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Methodology — choosing the right tool",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Validating a whole object with named fields? → BaseModel.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Validating a bare collection / TypedDict / union, no model needed? → TypeAdapter.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Reshaping raw input before typing? → @field_validator(mode=\"before\") or a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "model mode=\"before\" validator.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cross-field business rule on typed data? → @model_validator(mode=\"after\").",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Same validation reused across models/types? → Annotated[T, AfterValidator(...)].",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A union you can tag? → discriminated union (Field(discriminator=...)).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "App configuration? → BaseSettings from pydantic-settings.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Need exact types, no coercion (e.g. money, ids)? → strict=True (per-field or model).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#methodology-choosing-the-right-tool",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Practical Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Parse, don't validate-then-pass-dicts: convert at the boundary",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(Model.model_validate_json(body)) and pass typed models inward.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PATCH/partial update: model_dump(exclude_unset=True) to send only fields the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Aliases for external naming: `Field(validation_alias=\"userId\",",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "serialization_alias=\"user_id\"); set populate_by_name=True` to also accept the",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Python field name on input.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Immutable value objects: model_config = ConfigDict(frozen=True) → hashable,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "usable as dict keys / in sets.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Bulk validation: build one module-level TypeAdapter(list[Model]) and call",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "validate_python once on the whole batch rather than looping per item.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Context-aware validation: Model.model_validate(data, context={...}), read via",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "info.context in validators (e.g. inject locale, feature flags).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#practical-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns (and the fix)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Overusing @field_validator for simple bounds. A Python validator always runs in",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Python (function-call overhead, duplicates checks). → Use Annotated[int, Field(ge=0)]",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "so the constraint runs in Rust.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "mode=\"before\" when you wanted typed data. Before-validators get raw input",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(often a str/dict), causing AttributeError/type bugs. → Use mode=\"after\" for",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "rules on validated values.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Building a TypeAdapter inside a hot loop / per request. It recompiles the core",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "schema each time. → Construct once at module scope and reuse.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "json.loads() then model_validate(dict). → model_validate_json(raw) parses",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "and validates in one Rust pass.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "v1 carry-overs: class Config (→ model_config = ConfigDict(...)), @validator",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(→ @field_validator), @root_validator (→ @model_validator), .dict()",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(→ .model_dump()), .json() (→ .model_dump_json()), parse_obj (→ model_validate),",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "parse_raw (→ model_validate_json), from_orm/orm_mode",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(→ model_validate(obj) + from_attributes=True), allow_mutation=False",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "(→ frozen=True), each_item=True (→ annotate the inner type).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Mutable default shared across instances (tags: list = []). → Field(default_factory=list).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Mixing Pydantic v1 and v2 models in one validation graph - they don't nest cleanly;",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "migrate the whole graph (bump-pydantic), or use the pydantic.v1 shim deliberately.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Expecting validate_assignment by default. It's off; set",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "ConfigDict(validate_assignment=True) if you mutate after construction.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#anti-patterns-and-the-fix",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Troubleshooting",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "ValidationError - iterate exc.errors() for structured dicts (loc, msg,",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "type, input); exc.json() / exc.error_count() for reporting. The type",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "string (e.g. int_parsing, missing, string_too_short) is the stable machine key.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Input should be a valid integer\" under strict mode - you passed a string to a",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "strict int; coerce upstream or drop strictness for that field.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Serialization warning \"Expected X but got Y\" - a field's runtime value doesn't",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "match its declared type (common with Any/subclasses); set",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "model_dump(serialize_as_any=True) for duck-typed/polymorphic output, or fix the type.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "PydanticUndefinedAnnotation / forward refs - call Model.model_rebuild() after",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "the referenced type is defined (self-referential or late-bound models).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Settings not picked up - check env_prefix, the env_nested_delimiter, and that",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": ".env is found (relative to CWD unless an absolute env_file path is given).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "extra fields silently dropped - default is \"ignore\"; use \"forbid\" to catch",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "typos in input, \"allow\" to keep them.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pydantic-v2/#troubleshooting",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
